(text "PORT 4 — J5" (at 254.00000000000003 109.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "eea18eb4-b55b-5f53-ab3a-dd47fd56a579"))
(text "FOUR USB3 PORTS — SIGNAL-LINE ESD PROTECTION" (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c02c1ceb-1217-5681-a401-89c6358125c2"))
(text "One four-channel bidirectional TVS per port. Pins 1/2 protect TX; pins 4/5 protect RX. Both GND pins connect.\nTX protection is on the connector side of C1-C8. No connection to VBUS, D+ or D-. No supply pin is required." (at 15.24 185.42 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fec8198c-6b3f-5a7f-b6de-f5e2d93e7efa"))
(text "Pads 10/9/7/6 have no internal signal path. Route copper across pad pairs 1-10, 2-9, 4-7, 5-6.\nIdentical net labels do NOT provide an internal bridge. Place the array at the connector, with continuous pair routing\nand short ground returns. Avoid stubs and keep incoming ESD paths away from protected traces." (at 15.24 210.82 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d77bfc3e-2247-582a-890c-6c488f8998f1"))
(text "TI TPD4E02B04 SLVSD85B pp.3-5,15,24-25. Bidirectional +/-3.6V; not suitable for 5V VBUS protection.\n0.25pF typical / 0.33pF max per line at 0V, 1MHz, 25C. PCB/connector parasitics add to this.\nComponent ESD ratings do not establish board immunity. USB eye/return-loss and system ESD tests remain required." (at 15.24 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b9f24257-247e-56e5-83ed-9fee4abdeece"))
(embedded_fonts no))
